From: Harbottle & Lewis <litigation@harbottle-lewis.example> (Harbottle & Lewis, solicitors for RAM Media)
To: Mr Douvis <douvis@hellenic-culture-ministry.example> (Ministry of Culture, Organising Committee)
Date: 2006-10-30
Subject: RAM Media Limited - 2006 FIFPro Awards

We refer to your letter of 17th October. Our client has "beyond argument" fulfilled its obligations under the Agreement.

"We understand that you have now proposed to our client that you significantly reduce the amount that you agreed to pay to our client pursuant to the [Agreement] and that instead of releasing the bank guarantee in the sum of EUR 1.2 million and making further payments to our client of EUR 1.2 million and EUR 400,000 ... that instead you simply release a further EUR 1 million to our client .... Our client's position is that it would like to assist you if it can, but at present does not know whether or not this is possible. Our client owes obligations to FIFPro [PMG and others] ... Our client is reasonably optimistic that this will be possible ... In the meantime, timing is critical, and if funds are not released to our client by close of business today, our client will be unable to fund the broadcast of the event or retain the aircraft required to transport the players to the event. In those circumstances our client will have no option but to hold you in breach of contract ...

We must make it absolutely clear that if we do not have written confirmation from you by close of business today that the EUR 1.2 million in escrow has been released unconditionally to our client and is available for our client to spend, then the event will have to be cancelled and our client will resort to litigation against you".

Harbottle & Lewis

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: RAM Media v Ministry of Culture of the Hellenic Republic [2008] EWHC 1835 (QB), paras 141, 155.
Sent by fax at 14:05 London time. Proposals in the middle of the letter, including release of the bank guarantee, are not set out in the judgment; signatory not stated.
